<h2>Content pages</h2>
<p>Under <strong>Administration → Pages</strong>, pages such as the imprint, terms, privacy policy, withdrawal and report forms are made. A page has a language per text, a status (draft or published), a place in the header or footer, and can carry one of the legal roles. A legal role exists only once: only one page can be the imprint.</p>
<p>A language with no text of its own shows the default language's text.</p>

<h2>Media library</h2>
<p>Under <strong>Administration → Media library</strong>, pictures for the site are uploaded: JPEG, PNG or WebP up to 8 MB. Each picture is saved again (metadata removed, pictures over 2400 pixels scaled down) and gets a fixed address. The picker next to a text field inserts pictures from the library into page texts.</p>

<h2>Editing the home page, offer page and any content page in place</h2>
<p>The home page, the offer page (where a catalogue extension is running) and every content page made under <strong>Administration → Pages</strong> are made of the same block kit: a title area, text, latest offers, top providers, a picture, a link list, plus whatever extensions add on top (a photo gallery or a list of a certain offer type, for example). These blocks can be edited right on the page itself, not only through a form in the administration: a click on a text makes it editable, a "+" between two blocks inserts a new one. Blocks can be moved, hidden, removed, added and duplicated. A block used often can be saved as a widget of its own and inserted again later - on another page too.</p>
<p>Texts are edited in whichever language the header currently shows; the other languages stay as they are. Anyone who prefers a form instead finds the same blocks under <strong>Administration → Home page</strong> and <strong>Offer page</strong>, and a content page's blocks on its own edit page.</p>

<h2>Placeholders in text blocks</h2>
<p>Some extensions (the gallery or FAQ addon, for example) offer a <strong>placeholder</strong> of their own that can be typed into a text block on the home page or a page, such as <code>[gallery summer]</code> - once shown, it is replaced with whatever the extension produces for it (an album, an FAQ list, …). In edit mode the placeholder stays visible as plain text, so it is kept; on the published page only the result appears. Which placeholders are available is documented with the relevant extension.</p>

<h2>Design</h2>
<p>Under <strong>Administration → Design</strong>, the accent colour, background, text colour, font (four system font families) and corner radius are set. These values go into a small stylesheet of their own; the templates themselves stay untouched. The colours apply to the light colour scheme. The logo and the favicon are under <strong>Themes → Branding</strong>.</p>
